📅 Day 22 – File Handling in Java

Full Stack Web Development with Java Internship

Today’s session focused on File Handling in Java and how Java programs interact with files to store and retrieve data. The mentor explained how file operations allow applications to maintain persistent data outside the program.

🔹 Topics Covered
1️⃣ Introduction to File Handling

File handling allows programs to create, read, write, and delete files.

Java provides file handling support through the java.io package.

Files are commonly used for storing application data permanently.

2️⃣ File Handling Classes

The mentor introduced several classes used for file operations:

File → Used to create and manage file objects

FileReader → Reads character data from a file

FileWriter → Writes character data into a file

BufferedReader → Efficient reading of text files

BufferedWriter → Efficient writing of text files

3️⃣ File Operations Demonstrated

Creating a new file

Writing data into a file

Reading data from a file

Deleting a file

These operations help applications manage data storage effectively.

🔹 Practical Implementation

Created programs to generate a file using the File class.

Implemented file writing using FileWriter.

Read stored data using file reading classes.

Observed how Java handles file-based data storage.